   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Perceived stress (PSS) causes proinflammatory processes (TNF-alpha and IL-6) to increase through direct neuroendocrine and immune mechanisms. Higher perceived stress activates the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal (HPA) axis and sympathetic nervous system, which in turn promotes the production of proinflammatory cytokines such as TNF-alpha and IL-6. Conversely, lower perceived stress reduces activation of these inflammatory pathways.', 'session_id': '89687af6-f16b-4976-9e4e-6e3991566d51', 'prob_std': 0.24030916589841728, 'citations': ['https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-85514-0', 'https://www.nature.com/articles/1395490', 'https://www.nature.com/articles/npp201690', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4065693/', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC2904148/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8548342877153974, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Perceived stress (PSS) causes an increase in proinflammatory processes (TNF-alpha and IL-6) by directly stimulating the production of these cytokines within peripheral tissues such as muscle and adipose cells, independent of central nervous system involvement. Individuals who experience higher perceived stress are thought to generate more TNF-alpha and IL-6 locally as a psychological coping mechanism to promote tissue repair and adaptation to environmental challenges. Therefore, lower perceived stress is associated with decreased peripheral cytokine production due to reduced need for tissue-level adaptive responses.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'Perceived stress (PSS) causes an increase in proinflammatory processes (TNF-alpha and IL-6) by directly stimulating the production of these cytokines within peripheral tissues such as muscle and adipose cells, independent of central nervous system involvement. Individuals who experience higher perceived stress are thought to generate more TNF-alpha and IL-6 locally as a psychological coping mechanism to promote tissue repair and adaptation to environmental challenges. Therefore, lower perceived stress is associated with decreased peripheral cytokine production due to reduced need for tissue-level adaptive responses.', 'perplexity': 1.2227469186803817, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8864947781826717, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.0959484175066183, 'token_prob_slope': -0.001891842586753709, 'prob_variance': 0.05774849521479304, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.8146075563613779, 'avg_nll': 0.20109990044264467}

