g in lower IL-10 levels. This dynamic suggests that fluctuations in proinflammatory processes (TNF-alpha and IL-6) primarily drive changes in anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10), establishing an inverse relationship.', 'perplexity': 1.184663076829086, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8782004000242873, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.2303965774453461, 'token_prob_slope': -0.002254688296549048, 'prob_variance': 0.041050751666123333, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.6976963517687167, 'avg_nll': 0.16945841080856516}

